A. C. Tribble, B. Boyadjian, J. Davis, J. Haffner and E. McCullough. *Contamination Control Engineering Design Guidelines for the Aerospace Community*, NASA-CR-4740, May 1996. [Official catalogue](https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19960044619) · [Complete 132-page PDF](https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19960044619/downloads/19960044619.pdf).

Read the full report progressively: definitions, molecular films, particles, performance effects, control, monitoring, cleaning, storage and transport. Reconstruct the optical and thermal reasoning rather than transferring a cleanliness number to a different product. Chapters 2–3 require the quantitative and physical work introduced along the way.

On 30 October 2026 the catalogue, cover extraction, foreword, contents and selected particle-area passages were inspected. NTRS identifies the report as US-government work with public use permitted; retain component credits. Historical MIL-STD-1246C and FED-STD-209E references are part of this edition, not a claim about current standards. Assigned complete reading exceeds the passages inspected by the trail author. The document and its figures remain external.

